{"defects":[{"category":"concurrency/async-misuse","line":2,"explanation":"notify is declared `async def` but calls `client.post('/notify', ...)` without `await`. In an async client (the only reason for the async def), post returns a coroutine, so line 3's `response.status_code` raises AttributeError and the request is never actually sent (plus an un-awaited-coroutine warning). Either await the call or make the function synchronous."}]}
